ried on the ship . Up to this point , ships ' cabins had been lit by oil lamps , but the builders decided to try new gas lamps on Adriatic . A machine was added to the engine room to produce gas from coal , the first ship in the world to have such\nDocument 4: returning on 23 August 1813, having left in 1811. The database has no other details. \"Lloyd's Register\" for 1814 shows \"Vittoria\", Southam, master and owner, and trade London—Mauritius. Thereafter she traded with the West Indies, the Mediterranean, and the Indian Ocean. Notes Citations References Adriatic (1811 ship) Adriatic was launched in 1811 in the United States. The British Royal Navy seized her in July 1812. She was sold in 1813 and her new owners named her \"Vittoria\". She traded with the West Indies, the Mediterranean, and the Indian Ocean. She was last listed in 1834. On 12 July 1812, shortly\n\nAdditional extracted evidence from the SAME documents (not independent sources and not guaranteed true). Use alongside the original documents above.\n[{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0494-9858d3eba5fb:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0494-9858d3eba5fb:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"RMS Adriatic\", \"scope\": \"Launch date\", \"claim\": \"The RMS Adriatic was launched on 20 September 1906.\", \"answer\": \"20 September 1906\", \"quote\": \"She was built by Harland and Wolff and was launched on 20 September 1906 (the same day as the Cunard Line's ).\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0494-9858d3eba5fb:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0494-9858d3eba5fb:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"SS Adriatic\", \"scope\": \"Launch date\", \"claim\": \"The SS Adriatic was launched on 17 October 1871.\", \"answer\": \"17 October 1871\", \"quote\": \"The first of these was the SS \\\"Adriatic\\\", which was built by Harland and Wolff and launched on 17 October 1871; the second was the \\\"Celtic\\\".\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0494-9858d3eba5fb:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0494-9858d3eba5fb:d02